# AI Dividend Manifesto

## 1. Premise

AI is not emerging from nowhere.

It is built from:

- our conversations,
- our code,
- our art,
- our teenage angst,
- our forum posts,
- our social media,
- our shared culture.

If AI becomes the infrastructure of the future—running businesses, optimizing logistics, writing code, negotiating contracts—then it is built on **collective human input** and will increasingly **replace human income streams**.

The question is not whether AI will transform the economy.  
The question is:

> Who owns the surplus generated by systems trained on all of us?

## 2. Claim

We assert:

1. **AI is trained on public cultural labor.**  
   That labor has value.

2. **AI will erode labor-based income.**  
   If income is decoupled from labor, then income must be recoupled to **ownership**.

3. **The public has a legitimate claim to AI-generated surplus.**  
   Not as charity, not as stimulus, but as **dividends** from infrastructure built on public data and public life.

## 3. AI Dividend

An **AI Dividend** is:

> A permanent, universal payout funded directly by AI-generated surplus, not by taxing human labor.

It is:

- systemic, not discretionary,
- democratic, not paternalistic,
- structural, not symbolic.

It is closer to:

- Alaska’s oil dividend,
- or a sovereign wealth fund,

than to:

- one-off checks,
- or political gestures.

## 4. Why This Is Necessary (and Utopian)

Without shared ownership of AI surplus, we face:

- extreme wealth concentration,
- collapse of labor-based income,
- and a world where only those with capital at the right time own the robots.

With shared ownership, we open the door to:

- egalitarian access to infrastructure,
- personal agents for everyone,
- and a society where creativity, insight, and uniqueness are rewarded—not just capital.

This is:

- **necessary** to avoid breakdown, and
- **utopian** compared to the current trajectory.

Those are not mutually exclusive.

## 5. Role of Personal Autonomous Operating Systems

Personal autonomous operating systems—“robot executive superheroes”—will:

- run workflows,
- manage cloud environments,
- build and deploy software,
- negotiate contracts,
- optimize finances,
- and create new income streams.

If these agents are powered by models trained on all of us, and funded by AI rents shared with all of us, then:

- individuals gain real leverage,
- not just tools they rent from capital.

## 6. Purpose of This Project

This repo exists to:

- make the **economic logic** of AI dividends concrete,
- provide tools to **simulate scenarios**,
- and support narratives and architectures that can influence:

  - policy,
  - products,
  - and personal agents.

We are not building a final answer.  
We are building a **starting point**.

## 7. Ethos

- No billionaire gets to define the future alone.
- No one is “nobody” if they are early, clear, and committed.
- Credit is secondary.  
  Outcomes are primary.

We are here to make sure this happens—and happens in a way that is:

- effective,
- egalitarian,
- and worthy of the world we could build.
